    <p>
      A contrast ad has to hold up to scrutiny, so the motion design started
      with the public record: local news coverage and the port's own
      investigation report. The key quotes and passages were pulled out and kept
      on screen with their sources.
    </p>
    <p>
      To keep a dense story memorable, the spot is built as an animated paper
      collage: newspaper clippings, torn-out quotes, boarding passes and a
      travel postcard for the spending story. It lands on one line, "Residents
      of the Port of Benton deserve better," with the required paid-for
      disclaimer in place.
    </p>
